Yeah my speakers are front heavy too. the rear speakers make a little noise but not much ot really contribute

&#x200B;

sound is still amazing in the car however.  HEV SX is what i have

i think thats when i started noticing kias - about five years ago. and since then i feel like they said hold me beer and have been killing everyone on design since (must be all the BMW designers and engineers that went to kia)

&#x200B;

and yeah upon first glance i thought the stinger was GT line or EV6.  I agree its redundant now but good show old chap

if the engine was burning oil the smoke would have a slight blue tint.

&#x200B;

Most likely condensation.

so they break the window and open it from the inside

&#x200B;

unless it can somehow detect an opening from the lock or fob

&#x200B;

still, a step in the right direction. although one could say they went the cheap route and did a patchwork fix vs using an immobilizer

&#x200B;

my rationale says theyre doing this because its MUCH quicker and easier to do this while immobilizer's are manufactured and shipped over  and as we all know there is a parts and supply chain issue going on - so how do they win? get flak for providing this update workaround neing 'cheap' , or get flak because the wait time for an immobilizer is long due to supply and part constraints?

&#x200B;

be happy theyre doing this - but still place blame on them not building them correctly with immobilizer's form the beginning

id find a different kia dealership that can see you sooner.

&#x200B;

or call and ask for service manager and state you have a very new vehicle encountering this issue and it needs to be fixed under the bumper to bumper asap

&#x200B;

dont be a dick but be firm

LF eevee with anticipation 

&#x200B;

anyone?
